Alembic migration environment for PostgreSQL persistence.

Step 5.3 initializes this environment without adding a revision or creating a
database object. Schema revisions begin in Step 5.4. Database URLs are never
stored in alembic.ini or revision files; env.py reads the selected target from
the typed PLP_* settings at runtime.

Set `PLP_ENVIRONMENT=development` to use `PLP_DATABASE_URL` or
`PLP_ENVIRONMENT=test` to use `PLP_TEST_DATABASE_URL`. Production migration
access requires both `PLP_ENVIRONMENT=production` and the separate TLS-required
`PLP_PRODUCTION_MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL`. The hosted API uses
`PLP_PRODUCTION_DATABASE_URL` instead and never receives the migration URL.
